Inkless Kafka is Aiven's Apache Kafka fork introducing an storage sub-system for _Diskless_ topics.
Compared to _Classic_ topics, Diskless topics do not rely on the local filesystem and Kafka replication, 
but move that responsibility to a distributed remote storage system (e.g. AWS S3).

> This fork is an implementation for the KIP-1150 proposal which is being voted by the community,
> and should inspire the upstreaming of this feature if adopted.

Having worked on this codebase for more than a year now and iterated on some of its features,
it feels like a good time to start sharing more about it.

